<!----><h3>Before disguising</h3><!---->
[[File:Neeko Disguise Menu HUD.png|300px|right|thumb|Disguise menu on the HUD]]
* '''Neeko's''' disguise collection is offered through a special ''Disguise Menu'' in the HUD. The menu holds up to 5 ''slots'', based on the number of allied {{tip|champions}}. The player can select a disguise by {{LMB}} clicking on their portrait or via the Champion Specific Interaction [[hotkey]]s (default: {{sbc|Shift}}+{{sbc|F1–F5}}). The ''Sho'Ma'' disguise can be discarded by clicking on the 'x' next to the disguise's icon or via the sixth Champion Specific Interaction hotkey (default: {{sbc|Shift}}+{{sbc|F6}}).
** The ''slot'' containing her ''Sho'Ma'' disguise will be third in the HUD if there are two or more allied champions in the game, otherwise it will be the rightmost ''slot''. The remaining ''slots'' will contain allied champion disguises in order of their appearance in the pre-game [[Loading Screen]].
* Casting '''Inherent Glamour''' does not count as an ability activation for the purposes of on-cast effects such as {{tip|Spellblade}}, {{ais|Force Pulse|Kassadin}} passive, and does not interrupt {{ai|Shapesplitter|Neeko|the clone's}} movement orders.
* '''Neeko''' does not begin storing ''Sho'Ma'' from a unit if that unit enters her {{tip|sight}} and gathering range at the same time, or if it is within gathering range when she loses the disguise.
* The progress of gathering ''Sho'Ma'' from a unit is not lost even if '''Neeko''' stores ''Sho'Ma'' from a different unit.
* ''Inherent Glamour's'' cooldown only prevents '''Neeko''' from activating disguises; she can still store and remove ''Sho'Ma'' while the passive is on cooldown.
* When disguising while storing ''Sho'Ma'' from a unit, '''Neeko''' continues to store ''Sho'Ma'' from that unit.
* '''Neeko''' cannot store ''Sho'Ma'' from {{ai|Dark Procession|Yorick}} and {{ai|Powder Keg|Gangplank}}.
<!--is this true? * Storing ''Sho'Ma'' from {{ai|Demacian Standard|Jarvan IV}}{{bug}} will require '''Neeko''' to begin storing ''Sho'Ma'' from another unit, then move into proximity of the flag.-->
* After successfully storing ''Sho'Ma'', Neeko celebrates by clapping.
** This animation is forced and overrides all other animations except {{ais|Pop Blossom|Neeko}} landing animation.
* If '''Neeko''' attempts to activate a disguise while near the {{tip|stealthed trap|trap}}, {{tip|ward}}, or [[jungle plants|jungle plant]] she stored ''Sho'Ma'' from, she will {{tip|lunge|leap}} to that unit's exact position over 1 second, though not through terrain, and then become disguised. If she does so for a monster and is near its respective jungle camp, she will leap to that monster's usual position in the camp.
** If the monster is any {{ui|Krug}}, she will leap to the ''large'' Krug's position in the camp on the blue side or ''medium'' Krug's position on the red side.
** If the monster is {{ui|Rift Scuttler}} or a ''lesser'' {{ui|Raptor}}, she will leap to its position at the time of storing ''Sho'Ma'' instead.{{bug}}
** The leap is interrupted if '''Neeko''' attacks, moves, or casts certain abilities and spells.
*** The disguise will still activate after 1 second if the leap is interrupted by moving or attacking.
** '''Neeko''' cannot gather ''Sho'Ma'' while leaping.
** She will fail to activate the disguise after the leap if she is affected by the same conditions that would break a disguise.
** ''Inherent Glamour's'' leap has a number of interactions that set it apart from other {{tip|lunge|lunges}}:
**# ''Inherent Glamour's'' leap does not interact with {{iis|Voltaic Cyclosword}} {{nie|Galvanize}} passive;
**# ''Inherent Glamour's'' leap does not override the forced movement inflicted by {{tip|airborne}} effects;
**# The path of ''Inherent Glamour's'' leap will be similar to the path '''Neeko''' would take if ordered to move to the unit's position instead.
<!--it is still a lunge however, because a professional lunge expert told us so (it uses some kind of move block or something)-->
** '''Neeko''' will copy the unit's facing direction when disguising after leaping.
** If '''Neeko''' does not arrive at the unit's position while leaping, she will continue moving toward it.
* While not disguised, attempting to cast ''Inherent Glamour'' during a cast time or {{tip|attack windup}} puts the ability on cooldown immediately, but postpones the disguise.
** Doing so while disguised will not postpone the effect and will interrupt the {{tip|attack windup}}.
** This allows '''Neeko''' to successfully disguise even if she gets affected by effects that would put ''Inherent Glamour'' on cooldown during the delay.{{bug|2}}
* '''Neeko''' can activate ''Inherent Glamour'' while {{tip|channel|channeling}}, and remain in the disguise during the channel.{{bug|2}}
* '''Neeko''' can activate ''Inherent Glamour'' while {{tip|immobilize|immobilized}}, and remain in the disguise during the immobilization, despite the fact that immobilizations are meant to break the disguise.{{bug|2}}
<!--see next patch if this is real lol * Casting ''Inherent Glamour'' while channeling {{si|Hexflash}} causes ''Hexflash'' to be recast early.-->
<!----><h3>While disguised</h3><!---->
* '''Neeko''' will copy aesthetics as well as superficial mechanical [[Champion statistic|statistics]]. She will fake a number of readings:
** [[Health|Health bar]] (original's current amount becomes her apparent maximum)
*** While disguised as {{ci|Kled}}, '''Neeko's''' health bar simulates a [[Health#Health_threshold|health threshold]], but does not color '''{{uis|Skaarl|nolink=true}}''' {{as|health}} properly.{{bug}}
** [[Ability Resource|Secondary resource]] - e.g. {{as|mana}}, {{as|energy}} or none at all (original's current amount becomes her apparent maximum)
*** If disguised as a {{ui|Blue Siege Minion|Siege  Minion}}, '''Neeko''' cannot see her mana bar.{{bug}}
** [[Ammunition]]
** [[Champion statistic|Stats]]
** {{tip|Buff|Buffs}} and {{tip|Debuff|debuffs}} with their respective icons and VFX/SFX (there are exceptions)
*** '''Neeko''' sees the buffs that are actually applied to her, while enemies see the disguise's form's buffs.
**** Although '''Neeko''' can see the buffs, she cannot read their descriptions by hovering their icons.{{bug}}
**** After gaining a charge of {{nie|Shared Riches}} ({{ii|World Atlas}}, {{ii|Runic Compass}}), '''Neeko''' is unable to see the charge count until she consumes a charge.{{bug}}
** [[Experience (champion)|Level]]
** Kill feed icon
** Minimap icon
<!---->
* A number of attributes she actually adopts are:
** {{as|'''Base''' movement speed}} if it is lower than '''Neeko's''' {{as|'''base'''|movement speed}}
*** While disguised as a non-champion, '''Neeko's''' {{as|'''total''' movement speed}} cannot be reduced below {{as|200|movement speed}}.<!--any disguise, this increase/decrease is applied after everything else-->
*** While disguised as a ward or plant, '''Neeko's''' {{as|'''total''' movement speed}} cannot be increased above {{as|200|movement speed}}, except via effects that set {{as|movement speed}} to a certain value ({{ai|Chaaaaaaaarge!!!|Kled}}).<!--if you try with nami r it cuts out shortly after disguise, you also can't stack phage and pop ghost, maybe there's some exploit to do it tho-->
**** {{pending for test}} Is this true for traps?
** Classification of the unit (e.g. {{ui|Blue Melee Minion|melee}}, {{ui|Blue Siege Minion|siege}} minion; large, small monster; ward)
*** '''Neeko''' is never considered a minion for the purposes of {{ii|Reinforced Armor (Turret Item)|Reinforced Armor}}.
** {{tt|Base range type of the unit ({{tip|melee}}, {{tip|ranged}})|does not inherit transformations that change the range classification, with exceptions}}
*** {{tip|Wards}}<!-- and {{ui|Blood Rose|icononly=true}}{{ui|Large Blood Rose|Blood Roses}}--> are considered to be melee, while [[jungle plants]] and {{ui|Rift Scuttler}} are considered to be ranged.
*** When disguising as {{ci|Nidalee}} in {{ai|Aspect of the Cougar|Nidalee|Cougar Form}} or {{ci|Elise}} in {{ai|Spider Form|Elise|Spider Form}}, '''Neeko''' is special cased to become {{tip|melee}}.
** {{as|'''Base''' attack speed}} and attack ratio
*** When disguising as a non-champion, '''Neeko''' instead has her {{as|'''total''' attack speed}} set to that of the disguise's form, or to {{fd|2.0}} if the disguise's form's {{as|'''total''' attack speed}} is any higher.
*** Although {{ci|Jhin}} gains additional base attack speed through [[growth]], '''Neeko''' only inherits his level 1 base attack speed value.{{bug}}
** {{tip|Basic attack}} damage type ({{tip|basic damage}}, {{tip|ability damage}}), and subtype ({{tip|physical damage|{{as|physical damage}}}}, {{tip|magic damage|{{as|magic damage}}}})
*** For example, many {{tip|pets}} deal ability damage instead of basic damage with their basic attacks.
**** However, {{tip|critical strikes}} from non-champions always deal {{as|physical}} basic damage.
** The {{tip|projectile}} or non-projectile quality of their attack and projectile speed, if applicable
*** When {{tip|critical strike|striking critically}} as a non-champion with a projectile attack, the attack projectile is invisible and hits near-instantly, but can still be intercepted by {{ai|Wind Wall|Yasuo}} and similar abilities.
** {{sti|attack range|'''Base''' attack range}} of the unit's base form
*** For example, in the case of {{ci|Gnar}}, she will adopt {{tt|{{ccd|Gnar|range}}|Gnar's base range}} attack range.
*** When disguising as {{ci|Nidalee}} in {{ai|Aspect of the Cougar|Nidalee|Cougar Form}} or {{ci|Elise}} in {{ai|Spider Form|Elise|Spider Form}}, '''Neeko''' is special cased to adopt {{tt|125 range|the range they gain when they transform}} as her base range.
** Damage dealt to champions ({{as|physical|physical damage}}, {{as|magical|magic damage}}) ratio for the purposes of {{cai|Adaptive Defenses|Camille}}.
** {{tip|Size}} (including size modifiers and base unit size) at the time of disguising
** {{tip|Pathing radius}} when disguising as a non-champion
*** {{pending for test}} Is the same true for champions?
** Voice lines
** Base unit model, not accounting for the unit's current except in {{tt|special cases|see the visual effects section}}
<!-- possible trivia? *** The exception are ''Voidborn'' forms of {{ui|Blue Sentinel}} and {{ui|Red Brambleback}}, whose models '''Neeko''' does adopt --><!--does not work for void scuttle :(-->
** Default transformation toggle (non-innate)
** Character interactions (jokes, taunts, dances, laughs, toggle effects), as well as their {{si|Recall}} animation
*** '''Neeko''' can copy {{cis|Samira}} taunt animation but she will not actually throw the coin via the {{ai|Taunt|Samira|image = Samira splash coin.png}} ability.
*** While disguised as a non-champion, '''Neeko''' will play her laugh sound when attempting to laugh.
*** {{note|1}} This is an intentional feature, requested by fans when '''Neeko's''' [[V13.9]] gameplay update was released.
**** While disguised as a {{ai|We Are More|Naafiri|''Packmate''}}, she will play {{cis|Naafiri}} laugh instead.
