** '''Neeko''' will fail to purchase these items when disguising as a unit of required level if her real level is lower than required.
<!----><h3>Breaking the disguise</h3><!---->
* ''Inherent Glamour's'' disguise is broken by the following actions:
** Casting {{ai|Q|Neeko}} or {{ai|E|Neeko}}.
*** Casting {{ai|R|Neeko}} will not break the disguise immediately, but after a delay.
** Using {{si|Exhaust}}, {{si|Ignite}}, {{si|Smite}}, {{si|Unleashed Smite}}, {{si|Primal Smite}}, or {{si|Mark}}.
*** Using {{si|Dash}} will not break the disguise.
** Activating the following items:
*** {{ii|Hextech Gunblade}}
*** {{ii|Hextech Rocketbelt}}
*** {{ii|Profane Hydra}}
*** {{ii|Randuin's Omen}}
*** {{ii|Ravenous Hydra}}
*** {{ii|Redemption}}
*** {{ii|Stridebreaker}}
*** {{ii|Tiamat}}
*** {{ii|Titanic Hydra}}
* While disguised as a champion{{bug|2}}, dealing {{tip|ability damage}} to champions with abilities or items will also break the disguise.
* {{cai|Comeuppance|Akshan}} is special cased to break the disguise and put it on a 2-second cooldown both before damaging '''Neeko''' and while targeting her.
* Damage dealt by {{ui|Voidmite|Voidmites}} summoned by '''Neeko''' will be attributed to '''Neeko''' and will break the disguise if the disguise's form is a non-champion.{{bug|2}}
** This includes Voidmites summoned by [[File:Rift Herald Rodeo buff.png|Rift Herald Rodeo|20px|link=Rift Herald#Summoned form]] [[Rift Herald#Abilities|Rift Herald Rodeo]] if Rift Herald was {{tip|attached}} to '''Neeko''' during the charge.
